---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CardGrid from '../../../components/CardGrid.astro';
import DocCard from '../../../components/DocCard.astro';
const sidebar = [
  { title: 'Documentation Home', href: '/docs' },
  { title: 'Detection Overview', href: '/docs/detection' },
  { title: 'Detection Capabilities', href: '/docs/detection/capabilities', active: true },
  { title: 'Seeded CVEs', href: '/docs/detection/cves' },
  { title: 'Suricata Network IDS', href: '/docs/detection/suricata' },
  { title: 'Pattern Database', href: '/docs/detection/patterns' },
  { title: 'Advanced Signals', href: '/docs/detection/advanced' },
  { title: 'Device & GDPR Signature', href: '/docs/detection/signature' },
];
const toc = [
  { id: 'summary', text: 'Capability Summary', level: 2 },
  { id: 'signals', text: 'Signal Families', level: 2 },
  { id: 'techniques', text: 'Detection Techniques', level: 2 },
  { id: 'cve', text: 'CVE Pattern Matching', level: 2 },
  { id: 'functions', text: 'Function Reference', level: 2 },
  { id: 'honest', text: 'Honest Assessment', level: 2 },
];
---
<DocsLayout title="Detection Capabilities" description="What the system can detect and how it identifies malicious activity" section="Detection" sidebar={sidebar} toc={toc}>
  <h2 id="summary">Capability Summary</h2>
  <p>The system provides detection coverage across multiple analytical layers, implemented across <code>pattern_rules.lua</code>, <code>vulnerability_rules.lua</code>, <code>suricata_rules.lua</code>, <code>abuseipdb_rules.lua</code>, <code>session_rules.lua</code>, <code>upload_rules.lua</code>, <code>admin_rules.lua</code>, and <code>sophistication_analyzer.lua</code>.</p>

  <h2 id="signals">Signal Families</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <DocCard
      title="Request shape"
      icon="code"
      tag="pattern_rules"
      description="Generic and specific URI patterns, URL-encoding evasion, parameter pollution, request methods and header anomalies."
      meta="+5 … +80 per match"
    />
    <DocCard
      title="Known vulnerabilities"
      icon="shieldAlert"
      tag="vulnerability_rules"
      description="Exact matching of seeded CVE exploit signatures against the URI, query arguments and required headers."
      meta="+40 per CVE"
    />
    <DocCard
      title="Network evidence"
      icon="network"
      tag="suricata_rules"
      description="eve.json alert extraction, severity mapping, private-address filtering and time-decayed reputation."
      meta="+10 … +50 per alert"
    />
    <DocCard
      title="Session behaviour"
      icon="activity"
      tag="session_rules · admin_rules"
      description="Brute force, repeated admin attempts, automation fingerprints, request-rate streaks and cumulative suspicion."
      meta="Thresholds and streaks"
    />
    <DocCard
      title="Uploads and tokens"
      icon="key"
      tag="upload_rules · honeytoken_rules"
      description="AJAX upload analysis, dangerous content types and detection of injected fake credentials appearing inbound."
      meta="High-confidence signals"
    />
    <DocCard
      title="Reportability"
      icon="clipboard"
      tag="abuseipdb_rules"
      description="Deterministic mapping from routing reasons to AbuseIPDB categories, with matched CVEs in the report comment."
      meta="6 reason types"
    />
  </CardGrid>

  <table>
    <tr><th>Capability</th><th>Technique</th><th>Module</th><th>Description</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Direct CVE Matching</td><td>Lua URI/argument patterns</td><td>vulnerability_rules.lua</td><td>Exact matching of seeded CVE exploit signatures</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Generic Attack Patterns</td><td>Lua pattern signatures</td><td>pattern_rules.lua</td><td>Heuristic coverage for SQLi, XSS, C2, injection, traversal, upload abuse</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Network IDS</td><td>Suricata signatures</td><td>suricata_rules.lua</td><td>Alert-based detection correlated via suricata_rules</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Behavioral Signals</td><td>Brute force, automation, anomalies</td><td>session_rules.lua</td><td>Session anomaly detection, automation detection via UA fingerprint and timing</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Reportability</td><td>AbuseIPDB mapping</td><td>abuseipdb_rules.lua</td><td>Deterministic gating and comment enrichment with matched CVEs</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Sophistication Classification</td><td>Weighted rule set</td><td>sophistication_analyzer.lua</td><td>Classifies traffic as scripted / ai_assisted / manual / unknown</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Honeytoken Detection</td><td>Token corpus scanning</td><td>honeytoken_handler.lua</td><td>Detects when injected fake credentials appear in inbound requests</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2 id="techniques">Detection Techniques</h2>
  <h3>Pattern Matching</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Generic patterns</strong>: Layer 1 entries in <code>pattern_rules.SUSPICIOUS_PATTERNS</code> — each entry declares how it matches (plain, ext, param, segment, pat). Matches add +15 per entry.</li>
    <li><strong>Specific checks</strong>: Layer 2 in <code>pattern_rules.analyze_uri_patterns()</code> with per-pattern scores (directory traversal +20, SQL drop +30, wp-config.bak +80).</li>
    <li><strong>URL encoding evasion</strong>: +10 when percent-encoding is detected in the URI.</li>
    <li><strong>HTTP Parameter Pollution</strong>: +15 when more than 20 parameters are present.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Header Analysis</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Flagged User-Agents</strong>: +50 for known automation/scanner tools (sqlmap, nmap, masscan, zap, acunetix, nikto, dirb, gobuster, wpscan, whatweb, nuclei, burpsuite, havij, pangolin).</li>
    <li><strong>Missing User-Agent</strong>: +10 — legitimate browsers always send one.</li>
    <li><strong>CVE-2023-28121 header</strong>: +50 when <code>X-WCPAY-PLATFORM-CHECKOUT-USER</code> is present.</li>
    <li><strong>Missing Referer on POST</strong>: +5 (WSTG-ATHN-04).</li>
    <li><strong>HTTP Basic Authentication probe</strong>: +5.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="cve">CVE Pattern Matching</h2>
  <p><code>pattern_rules.analyze_cve_patterns()</code> checks URI, query string, and headers against <code>_G.config.vulnerability.cve_patterns</code>. Each match scores +40. See <a href="/docs/detection/cves">Seeded CVEs</a> for the full list.</p>

  <h2 id="functions">Function Reference</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Function</th><th>Module</th><th>Contract</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>analyze_uri_patterns(uri, args)</code></td><td>pattern_rules.lua</td><td>Returns a score delta plus the list of matched pattern names.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>analyze_header_patterns(headers)</code></td><td>pattern_rules.lua</td><td>Scores flagged or missing headers and CVE-specific header presence.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>analyze_cve_patterns(uri, args, headers)</code></td><td>pattern_rules.lua</td><td>Matches <code>config.vulnerability.cve_patterns</code>; +40 per CVE.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>detect_vulnerability_pattern(uri, args, header)</code></td><td>vulnerability_rules.lua</td><td>Returns <code>cve</code>, <code>severity</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>plugin</code> and <code>attack_vector</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>extract_alert(decoded)</code></td><td>suricata_rules.lua</td><td>Alert record, or <code>nil</code> for non-alert and malformed events.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>severity_to_score(severity)</code></td><td>suricata_rules.lua</td><td>1 → +50, 2 → +25, anything else → +10.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>is_reportable_reason(reason)</code></td><td>abuseipdb_rules.lua</td><td>True only for the six whitelisted routing reasons.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>classify_session(session)</code></td><td>sophistication_analyzer.lua</td><td>Class plus confidence for scripted / AI-assisted / manual / unknown.</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p>Individual module pages in the repository contain the complete function-level comments and their unit tests. The <a href="/docs/testing">testing</a> section lists the test file for each module.</p>

  <h2 id="honest">Honest Assessment</h2>
  <p><strong>Strengths:</strong> Explainable scoring, pure/adapter split for unit testing, severity-graded Suricata integration, NAT protection, sophistication classification, five honeytoken types and a consent-gated <a href="/docs/detection/signature">device signature</a> that survives a cookie wipe. A recorded exploit test-scenario run diverted 13/14 CVE exploits (and 14/16 plugin/theme targets) on the first request with no honeypot bypasses once routed — see <a href="/docs/testing#results">Validation Results</a>.</p>
  <p><strong>Limitations:</strong> Same-host Suricata testing gap, threshold tuning needed for legitimate API clients, generic pattern false positives (historical), no ML.</p>
</DocsLayout>
